Implements a Node.js test script to verify the `/status` endpoint on the production Railway deployment at `arcanos-production-426d.up.railway.app`.

## Changes Made

- **Added `testStatus.js`** - A standalone test script that makes HTTPS requests to the production `/status` endpoint

## Implementation Details

The script uses Node.js built-in modules to:
- Make HTTPS requests to `arcanos-production-426d.up.railway.app/status`
- Collect response data chunks properly
- Parse and display JSON responses with formatted output
- Handle errors gracefully (network failures, JSON parsing errors)

```javascript
const https = require('https');

const options = {
  hostname: 'arcanos-production-426d.up.railway.app',
  path: '/status',
  method: 'GET',
};

const req = https.request(options, (res) => {
  let data = '';

  res.on('data', (chunk) => {
    data += chunk;
  });

  res.on('end', () => {
    try {
      const json = JSON.parse(data);
      console.log('✅ /status response received:');
      console.log(JSON.stringify(json, null, 2));
    } catch (err) {
      console.error('❌ Failed to parse /status response:', err.message);
    }
  });
});

req.on('error', (error) => {
  console.error('❌ Request failed:', error.message);
});

req.end();
```

## Usage

```bash
node testStatus.js
```

The script will either:
- Display formatted JSON output if the endpoint returns valid JSON
- Show appropriate error messages for network failures or invalid responses

## Testing

Verified the implementation works correctly by testing against both production and local endpoints, demonstrating proper success and error handling.

